1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,900
We're not following you anymore.

2
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:17,900
Have you considered why you're having trouble responding to Smallfry's request?

3
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:20,100
Do you even want to put in the effort at all?

4
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:25,280
And if you can't understand that fact, you're every bit the despot king you used to be.

5
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:31,620
So, is there something the matter with Kageyama today?

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,940
Huh? There's nothing that I know of.

7
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:35,980
Well, nothing physically, anyway.

8
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:39,540
Hmm.

9
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:43,700
You know, I remember when Kageyama was in middle school,

10
00:00:44,060 --> 00:00:47,400
everyone kept talking about this up-and-coming genius setter in Miyagi,

11
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:49,480
who was apparently quite a sensation.

12
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:53,600
Personally, I thought he'd make the big jump in his third year of middle school,

13
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:55,440
but it looks like nothing ever happened.

14
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:57,580
A genius, huh?

15
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:00,960
I'm not sure what the actual definition for that is,

16
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:05,620
but personally, I think a genius is the farthest thing from perfect you can find.

17
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:10,060
And that is what makes a genius so interesting.

18
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:14,460
But on the court, well,

19
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:17,480
you're just a goody two-shoes.

20
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:23,600
爪痕が残るくらい

21
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:27,080
拳を固く握り締め

22
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:33,860
今オレンジの光の中へ

23
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:35,860
Oh, oh!

24
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:45,860
Ijiなく汗髪を引き裂く

25
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:48,860
満ちなるハイステージへ

26
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:51,860
Jorahway初めはね

27
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:54,860
抜かしていればいい

28
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:58,860
傷を恐れ羽ばたかぬ人生なんて

29
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:01,860
悪性と変わらない

30
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:03,860
人は一生

31
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:09,860
夢と感動くらい生きてく

32
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:13,860
痛いくらい羽根の腎臓

33
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:17,860
鳥肌が止まらない

34
00:02:17,860 --> 00:02:20,860
命が熱く燃えている

35
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:23,860
喧嘩着の先

36
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:28,860
その先で戦う喜びは

37
00:02:28,860 --> 00:02:34,860
勝ち負けすらもどこか遠く

38
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:38,860
時を止めたこの一瞬が

39
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:42,860
スローモーションで煌めく

40
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:46,860
さあ暴れな

41
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:56,860
勝ち負けすら

42
00:02:56,860 --> 00:02:58,860
勝ち負けすら

43
00:02:58,860 --> 00:03:00,860
勝ち負けすら

44
00:03:00,860 --> 00:03:02,860
勝ち負けすら

45
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:18,860
敵に対する

46
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:20,860
その方法で

47
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:22,440
Finish it!

48
00:03:23,820 --> 00:03:25,800
That was sloppy! And low!

49
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:27,160
Sorry about that.

50
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:30,480
Ugh, I hate overhand passes.

51
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:34,700
Nice to see Tsukishima getting yelled at for once.

52
00:03:35,660 --> 00:03:37,840
When there are only two of you on the court,

53
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:40,720
there's no one to compensate for your weaknesses.

54
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:45,440
On the return, they should be aiming for Hyakuzawa, right?

55
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:47,540
He caves way easier than Kunimi.

56
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:51,040
But then if Hyakuzawa does manage to get the ball back in the air,

57
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:53,320
he's going to be the one hitting it over the net.

58
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:56,480
And if the set is up high, he is definitely going to hit it.

59
00:03:57,040 --> 00:04:00,460
I mean, he is really good at slamming those high sets down.

60
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:03,500
He doesn't seem all that great at defense, but he's got a lot of stamina.

61
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:06,140
That, and he's got a really long reach.

62
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:09,000
So even when you're sure you're going to score, he gets to the ball.

63
00:04:17,540 --> 00:04:21,280
All right, here it goes!

64
00:04:21,420 --> 00:04:22,460
Take it real easy!

65
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:24,460
Thanks a lot, Hinata.

66
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:26,960
He really is a lot less stressed now.

67
00:04:28,020 --> 00:04:28,860
Finish it off!

68
00:04:30,540 --> 00:04:33,340
That's definitely not going to be an easy ball to hit.

69
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:36,240
Should I play back instead of jumping up to block?

70
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:37,220
No.

71
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:38,680
If I know Hyakuzawa,

72
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,580
he's going to go for the spike!

73
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:45,380
One touch!

74
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:48,300
Really nice job!

75
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:49,400
Good follow-through!

76
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:52,620
Crap.

77
00:04:52,940 --> 00:04:54,060
I think it drifted.

78
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:55,400
Whatever.

79
00:04:55,860 --> 00:04:56,660
It's good enough!

80
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:01,340
Oh, yeah!

81
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:02,880
Nice kill, man!

82
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:07,200
Tsukishima!

83
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:08,960
That was a nice set!

84
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:11,040
So what's with the face, then?

85
00:05:11,540 --> 00:05:13,940
I got to see you do some real setting for once,

86
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:15,420
which got me super excited,

87
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:17,280
but I hated to see you play better than me!

88
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:19,840
Well, thank you for the specific and honest opinion.

89
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:23,540
The pass I made wasn't even that good, though.

90
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:26,320
Yeah.

91
00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:27,440
I need...

92
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:30,720
I need to get better at everything, too!

93
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:34,640
Well, all right, then.

94
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:38,500
Coach Saito from Shira Torizawa Academy

95
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:39,640
is, uh...

96
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:40,780
not feeling well.

97
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:42,920
So we have a change of plans

98
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:44,620
and we'll be holding a practice match.

99
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:47,920
What happened to Coach Saito?

100
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:49,720
Heard he ate some bad oysters.

101
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:52,000
Mm-hmm.

102
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:55,900
So the third years and alumni from Shira Torizawa

103
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:57,380
will be playing as one team

104
00:05:57,380 --> 00:05:59,740
while the campers form the other team once again.

105
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:03,440
Today is the last day of your five-day camp,

106
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:05,720
so do your best to get better results

107
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:07,400
than you did in the previous scrimmage.

108
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:08,460
Oh!

109
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:11,540
The whole Shira Torizawa team!

110
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:13,800
Man, you don't get a chance like this every day!

111
00:06:14,660 --> 00:06:16,780
Come on, Kunimi, you're just as excited, right?

112
00:06:16,900 --> 00:06:17,520
Be honest!

113
00:06:17,780 --> 00:06:19,080
Secretly, you feel the same way!

114
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:19,840
You do!

115
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:20,620
You know you do!

116
00:06:20,620 --> 00:06:30,420
Come to think of it,

117
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:31,580
that kid from Karasuno,

118
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:33,780
he was ball boy the last time we did this too.

119
00:06:34,180 --> 00:06:35,360
Why isn't he out there playing?

120
00:06:35,620 --> 00:06:37,440
Uh, it's kind of complicated

121
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,680
and sort of a long story.

122
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:41,360
But for starters,

123
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:43,800
he wasn't actually asked to come to the training camp.

124
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:44,800
What?

125
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:46,240
How does that make sense?

126
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:55,400
Got it!

127
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:06,460
Ushiwaka!

128
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:06,980
Huh?

129
00:07:08,980 --> 00:07:10,300
Can I ask you a question?

130
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:13,620
Look, Hinata's actually talking to Ushiwaka.

131
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:15,180
He sure got some guts.

132
00:07:15,180 --> 00:07:16,960
You go to his school, don't you?

133
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:17,760
Well, yeah.

134
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:20,980
But that doesn't make him easy to talk to.

135
00:07:22,620 --> 00:07:24,440
What kind of stuff are you thinking about

136
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:26,060
when you set up to receive the ball?

137
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:29,240
Are you sure you don't want to go over there?

138
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:31,200
Maybe ask Ushiwaka for some tips?

139
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:33,140
After all, you never know

140
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:35,060
when we're ever going to see the guy again, right?

141
00:07:35,940 --> 00:07:37,560
Well, I, uh...

142
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:39,800
Asking a rival for his advice would be...

143
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:40,420
kinda lame.

144
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:42,660
Mmm.

145
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:51,460
No one should be able to say that much

146
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:52,300
with just their eyes.

147
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:54,720
Well, when it comes to taking initiative,

148
00:07:54,860 --> 00:07:56,360
there is one thing for certain here.

149
00:07:57,260 --> 00:07:58,880
That number 10 from Karasuno

150
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:01,440
is definitely one step ahead of you already, at least.

151
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:08,880
Ushiwaka!

152
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:09,660
Oh.

153
00:08:09,660 --> 00:08:10,020
What the hell?

154
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:26,680
I'll be right back.

155
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:56,660
We'll be right back.

156
00:08:56,680 --> 00:09:26,660
We'll be right back.

157
00:09:26,660 --> 00:09:30,020
Akiyama's good on the left side, and Hoshiyumi's a great setter.

158
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:32,460
Yeah, he can play anywhere out there.

159
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:35,700
You get some interesting results when you shuffle people around.

160
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:40,640
I'm on a roll.

161
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:44,060
They're all so good, and they're lifting me up.

162
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:45,740
Coming at ya!

163
00:09:45,740 --> 00:09:52,540
Man, that was great.

164
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:57,040
Nice shot!

165
00:09:57,920 --> 00:10:00,400
Hey, you just doubted that my set was good, didn't you?

166
00:10:01,060 --> 00:10:02,880
I was taking a second to be sure.

167
00:10:03,020 --> 00:10:04,040
Can't be too careful.

168
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:05,820
I'm impressed.

169
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,880
This guy can play any position.

170
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:12,080
More than anything, this is the time to find hidden talents.

171
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:15,720
You never know where we might discover some kind of ripe new potential.

172
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:19,600
And we don't know what the players themselves might learn from this.

173
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:22,200
Sooner or later, their day will come.

174
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:26,900
The day when these gifted athletes are going to have to prove their worth, prove their skills.

175
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:33,940
But I want these boys to always enjoy playing volleyball, no matter what kind of pressure they're under.

176
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:35,920
It's still a game, after all.

177
00:10:37,420 --> 00:10:40,920
And it might sound incredibly cliche to tell them to take their time.

178
00:10:42,060 --> 00:10:45,040
But, well, it's important advice.

179
00:10:45,700 --> 00:10:46,640
There's no rush.

180
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:51,800
Mia!

181
00:10:52,140 --> 00:10:53,400
Yeah, yeah, I got it.

182
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:55,800
Okay.

183
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:57,560
Here you go.

184
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:03,560
Yes!

185
00:11:04,220 --> 00:11:05,260
Nice kill, dude.

186
00:11:06,260 --> 00:11:09,740
A really good setter can cast a spell on his Spikers.

187
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:14,860
He can make his guys believe that they're better and stronger than they really are.

188
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:17,820
And we've got a really great crop of setters this year.

189
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:19,360
Hmm.

190
00:11:19,360 --> 00:11:27,180
I only hope the Spikers who have been getting sets from Kageyama Nutsumu don't get too confused when they have to go back to their home teams.

191
00:11:27,180 --> 00:11:29,060
Oh, my God!

192
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:32,940
Mm-hmm.

193
00:11:32,940 --> 00:11:34,200
Which is kind of cool.

194
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:48,720
Mm-hmm.

195
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:49,360
Hmm.

196
00:11:52,620 --> 00:11:53,860
Huh?

197
00:11:53,860 --> 00:11:54,540
Huh?

198
00:11:54,540 --> 00:11:58,320
Nice serve! Well done!

199
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:02,560
He says she's gotten really good at jump float serves.

200
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:04,920
I have to keep up.

201
00:12:11,060 --> 00:12:13,520
It's a bit long, but it's getting better.

202
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:16,060
Um, thanks!

203
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:18,400
Noya! Here I come!

204
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:19,860
Alright, bring it on!

205
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:21,440
Coach!

206
00:12:22,420 --> 00:12:24,140
Hey, out of go, Specs.

207
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:25,480
They really like the idea.

208
00:12:26,420 --> 00:12:27,280
Do it again!

209
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:29,220
Now we just have to find a time that works.

210
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:30,760
Alright.

211
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:34,260
Spring Nationals are coming in less than a month.

212
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:38,540
So I want to play as many matches as we can once our full lineup's back.

213
00:12:39,520 --> 00:12:41,860
Against the strongest opponents we can get.

214
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:42,740
Agreed.

215
00:12:44,360 --> 00:12:46,540
And as of tomorrow, we'll have them back.

216
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:48,600
The whole team.

217
00:12:50,260 --> 00:12:51,920
So, how'd you like being a Spiker?

218
00:12:52,900 --> 00:12:54,260
I found it interesting.

219
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:57,300
And the sets you gave me were really easy to work with as well.

220
00:12:57,580 --> 00:12:58,480
Yeah, I know, right?

221
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:03,760
Anyone who can't hit one of my sets is a real waste of space.

222
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:07,520
But anyway, I wanted to ask you.

223
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:09,560
Are you sure you wouldn't rather be a Spiker?

224
00:13:09,780 --> 00:13:11,180
Uh, why would you ask that?

225
00:13:11,340 --> 00:13:14,860
You've just had this real tense look on your face every time you've made a set.

226
00:13:15,660 --> 00:13:21,780
Yeah, well, that probably has something to do with the fact that you called him a goody two-shoes buddy.

227
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:25,020
But then, it went away while you were playing on the wing.

228
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:26,500
You think so?

229
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:28,700
But I'm not a Spiker.

230
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:29,380
I'm a setter.

231
00:13:30,180 --> 00:13:30,420
Hmm.

232
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:32,160
Yeah, I guess you are.

233
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:35,840
Uh, so, uh, tell me something.

234
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:36,660
Hmm?

235
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:40,420
What was it you meant before, calling me goody two-shoes?

236
00:13:41,060 --> 00:13:41,300
Hmm?

237
00:13:42,140 --> 00:13:43,460
Exactly what it sounds like.

238
00:13:44,020 --> 00:13:46,820
You're serious, obedient, and a real good boy.

239
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:47,700
Hmm.

240
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:56,260
You've been training with players you don't know in an unfamiliar gym.

241
00:13:56,800 --> 00:13:58,440
And you've all done well.

242
00:13:58,820 --> 00:14:01,080
It's your first step toward the National Youth Team.

243
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:04,160
You may have felt like you were stumbling in the dark at times.

244
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:08,760
But I hope you don't think of your practices here as different than the practices you'll be doing back home.

245
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:11,540
Ideally, you should continue to lift each other up.

246
00:14:12,980 --> 00:14:14,940
Good luck, and keep working hard.

247
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:16,560
Been a pleasure, guys.

248
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:17,940
Thank you very much, sir.

249
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:24,220
Kageyama, see you at Spring Nationals.

250
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:25,460
Yeah, see ya.

251
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:28,600
Later, man.

252
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:29,160
Hmm.

253
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:48,820
Kageyama, I'll see you around.

254
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:50,740
And best of luck in the Spring Nationals.

255
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:51,520
Thanks a lot.

256
00:14:58,300 --> 00:15:00,320
So, which way was the station?

257
00:15:01,620 --> 00:15:02,700
I'll walk you there.

258
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:04,700
Yes!

259
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:07,600
I get to play volleyball again tomorrow!

260
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,660
I'm gonna hit so many balls!

261
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:10,480
Ugh.

262
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:12,720
The training camp is finally over.

263
00:15:13,060 --> 00:15:14,680
And I still have to play tomorrow?

264
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:16,120
What is wrong with you?

265
00:15:16,460 --> 00:15:18,620
There's less than a month before Spring Nationals.

266
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:19,460
Yeah.

267
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:22,740
Getting the proper amount of rest is part of the training, too.

268
