321
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:31,320
Ah.

322
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:33,920
Having the two-on-two drills was a good idea.

323
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:34,760
Oh, good.

324
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:35,800
I'm glad you think so.

325
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:38,840
And Karasuno's number ten never even got to practice once?

326
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:40,300
No, just a ball boy.

327
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:41,620
Are you serious?

328
00:17:42,380 --> 00:17:42,700
Yep.

329
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:45,460
But he was more fired up than anyone else there.

330
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,760
And his enthusiasm definitely spread to the other kids.

331
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:49,240
Hmm.

332
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:53,240
Huh?

333
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:55,400
A need.

334
00:17:56,060 --> 00:17:59,080
An overpowering hunger for height.

335
00:18:00,620 --> 00:18:03,080
Whether you're actively aware of it or not.

336
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:06,800
Whether its presence inside you is something positive or something negative.

337
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:09,900
Deep down, that hunger is always there.

338
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:12,120
For both of us.

339
00:18:14,660 --> 00:18:17,940
What we've been given instead of physical stature

340
00:18:17,940 --> 00:18:20,500
is that driving hunger.

341
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:26,980
I am starving!

342
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:27,040
I am starving!

343
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:35,540
Thanks for waiting.

344
